{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-146850",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Note the following:\n\n- For a given joint PMF $f(x,y),$ we can think of each point where $f(x,y)\\ne 0$ as a point mass in the plane, where the \"probability mass\" at each point equals the probability associated with that point.\n\n- The joint CDF $F(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)$ is the total \"probability mass\" that lies in the infinite rectangular region that has its top-right corner at $(x,y)$ and whose sides are parallel to the coordinate axis.\n\nGiven the supports of $X$ and $Y,$ the joint support $S$ is a subset of\n\n$$\n{S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}\\times \\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's plot the points in ${S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y},$ which contains the joint support, and sketch the region corresponding to the probability we wish to find.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14201862/assets/6287f4884b335466bc7e1d6da17190f32d447f065e37a37e79a1aa48a6109415.png)\n\nNotice that this region encompasses the same possible support points as the rectangular region with its top-right corner at $(4,1)$ and bottom-left corner at $(2,-1)$ below, where the top and right boundaries are inclusive and the bottom and left boundaries are exclusive.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14201862/assets/d4d76ca2e80bccda9cbcfa4e28c628dffcec62b3fb42d62f9315fce2623e12fe.png)\n\nGeometrically, this region can be obtained as follows:\n\n1\\. Take the infinite rectangle that has its top-right corner at $(4,1).$\n\n2\\. Subtract the infinite rectangles that have their top-right corners at $(4,-1)$ and $(2,1).$\n\n3\\. Finally, we need to add back the infinite rectangle that has its top-right corner at $(2,-1).$ This is because we subtracted this region twice in step 2.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X<4,-1\\le Y<1) & =\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(4,1)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 4,Y\\le 1)}} \\\\  & \\,-\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(4,-1)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 4,Y\\le -1)}}-\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(2,1)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 2,Y\\le 1)}} \\\\  & \\,+\\overset{\\text{top-right corner at }(2,-1)}{\\overset{⏞}{P(X\\le 2,Y\\le -1)}} \\\\  & =F(4,1)-F(4,-1)-F(2,1)+F(2,-1) \\\\  & =0.8-0.2-0.3+0.1 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
